    "body": "## Background\nIn Mistral function call streaming detector, when no [TOOL_CALLS marker was present, the code still ran text.replace(\"]\", \"\") which corrupted any bracket characters in user normal text.\n\n## Problem\nStreaming responses like The item at items[0] has value [guide](url) would have all closing brackets stripped.\n\n## Solution\nRemoved the erroneous bracket-stripping logic. When there is no tool call marker, parse_streaming_increment should return text unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n- Reproduced the issue with the example from bug report\n- Verified items[0] and [guide](url) are now preserved correctly\n\nFixes #44219\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557289096](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557289096)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557288954](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557288954)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38557288992](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38557288992)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
